-- stdin
Take a sample of size n. Then compute the mean. See n. 4 for details.

The event has probability p. We estimate it. See p. 5 and pp. 6 for details.

The patient was ill. He recovered. See ill. 3 for details.

The size is in pt. If you print it, check pt. 2 first.

It takes one sec. Then read sec. 3 again.

Call the function f. Use distance d. Use constant c. It was built c. 1900 by hand.

See p.
5 for details.

(See p. 12) and "sec. 7" are references. The size is n.

Opening sentence. c. word follows. End.
